  over the 276 suppressed pairs only: mean 0.3937%  median 0.2851%  max 2.7062%

total resize notional that the dead zone would have avoided: 89,114.99 USDT
total gross traded across those anchors                    : 19,832,436.58 USDT
=> LOWER BOUND on turnover the dead zone would have saved  : 0.4493% of gross per anchor (mean)

AGAINST MEASURED TURNOVER of 2.0-5.5% of gross per anchor:
  unweighted mean 0.3721% of gross  =>  18.6% of the 2.0% end,  6.8% of the 5.5% end
  gross-weighted  0.4493% of gross  =>  22.5% of the 2.0% end,  8.2% of the 5.5% end

  i.e. had the dead zone bound, it would have removed on the order of a FIFTH to a
  FIFTEENTH of measured per-anchor turnover - a real but second-order saving, and a
  LOWER BOUND because it counts only the resize leg, not the per-name re-quoting that
  a changed gross induces downstream.
